n color; wall color (blue) forms barriers dividing the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-27-    - A unique single pixel (magenta) sits on one corner — the start marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-28-    - Some wall-colored pixels are structural (border-touching, enclosing regions); others are decorations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-29-\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-30-    Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-31-    - Flood-fill from the marker corner to find all reachable bg cells, blocked by structural walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-32-    - Erase wall-colored decorations hidden behind structural walls (not reachable from marker side).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-33-    - Paint orange (color 7) on every reachable bg cell adjacent to a wall or grid edge — forming a 1-cell inner border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-34-\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-35-    Key insight: Only border-connected wall components act as real barriers; interior wall fragments are decorations to be removed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-36-    \"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-37-    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-38-    h, w = g.shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-39-    bg = get_bg(g)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-40-\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-41-    out = g.copy()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-42-\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-43-    # Marker pixel is a unique (count==1) non-bg pixel on a corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-44-    counts = Counter(int(v) for v in g.ravel())\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f3a5a89.py-45-    corners = [(0, 0), (0, w - 1), (h - 1, 0), (h - 1, w 